Ã¦sarea, and there abode.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙêAnd Herod was highly displeased with them of Tyre and Sidon: but they came with one accord to him, and, having made Blastus the king's chamberlain their friend, desired peace; because their country was nourished by the king's country.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙgAnd upon a set day Herod, arrayed in royal apparel, sat upon his throne, and made an oration unto them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙPAnd the people gave a shout, saying, It is the voice of a god, and not of a man.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ…And immediately the angel of the Lord smote him, because he gave not God the glory: and he was eaten of worms, and gave up the ghost.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ(But the word of God grew and multiplied.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡And Barnabas and Saul returned from Jerusalem, when they had fulfilled their ministry, and took with them John, whose surname was Mark.¦layout ªlast_verse